<title>SINGAPORE: SINGAPORE EXCHANGE RATE APPROPRIATE, MAS SAYS.</title>
<headline>SINGAPORE EXCHANGE RATE APPROPRIATE, MAS SAYS.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The exchange rate of the Singapore dollar is appropriate to what is happening in the market, an official of the Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The official told a briefing the U.S. dollar had been rising in currency markets recently and the Singapore dollar had depreciated by about five percent against the U.S. unit since the start of 1997.</p>
<p>The MAS is Singapore's de-facto central bank.</p>
<p>The Singapore dollar was last at 1.4900/10 on Tuesday.</p>
</text>
